  2558	## 4. `SimplexFG.fj` — FJ root rule, own frame and interface (audit W06)
  2559	
  2560	FJ changes the frame rule: a frontier test, root F and band `{H}` in a
  2561	contest. It is a module variant, not a base selector. HNI is NOT the FJ
  2562	interface. FJ can keep a height-(M+1) source that does not extend an old
  2563	justified entry at M; this is a failure of HNI(M+1).(h1), while FJ's filter
  2564	still protects the source:
  2565	
  2566	> _fgsa-no-nj-opus.md, lines 612–620:_
  2567	>
  2568	> **N14: NJ-free reset — PROVED.** Under FJ every step of a descent chain
  2569	> has `x ≥ σ[C].h`. So every abandoned post-GST source has height at most
  2570	> M (§3.3). Every honest row at height ≥ M+1 has a synchronous label, so
  2571	> its source is extended by every honest HEAD from its label on. The next
  2572	> unanimous batch then puts it in every S by `t_s+10Δ` (fgsa-fast-opus
  2573	> §5.1 step 7). This is Lemma R with `x=M` and no NJ. It also follows the
  2574	> proof in fgsa-adjudicate §4: the only change is its "old J at x" clause.
  2575	> Under FJ an old J at M cannot pass a source C* at M+1, because C* is a
  2576	> frontier block that does not extend it.
  2577	
  2578	Thus `fg.HNI.v1`, `fg.H19.v1`, `fg.HNIb.v1`, `fg.trunk.v1`,
  2579	`fg.oneBullet.v1` (now `fg.oneBullet.core.v1`), `fg.base.finalized.v1`,
  2580	`fg.base.nj.v1` and `fg.baseSel.nj.v1` do not apply to FJ. The FJ
  2581	noninterference interface is `fj.descent.v1`, `fj.canonical.v1` (F9),
  2582	`fj.inBandLock.v1` (F10) and `fj.twoChanges.v1` (F12; now
  2583	`fj.twoChanges.core.v1` with `comp.settle.v1`); its reset witness is
  2584	`fj.reset.v1`. The `both` entries `fg.provenance.v2`,
  2585	`fg.causalCap.core.v1`, `fg.uniqueJust.v1`, `fg.finalLock.v1`,
  2586	`fg.frameCompat.v1`, `comp.provenance.v1`, `comp.settle.v1` and
  2587	`comp.cut.v1` apply to FJ. The FJ cap M
  2588	is the cap on old honest rows (`env.r148`); it is at most DC's archival
  2589	M0. r151 calls this cap μ and calls M0 simply M.
