   716	  `fBasis_lexMax`, plan `befb5d5`). Changed 2026-09-28; the earlier line
   717	  was "none".
   718	- Hypotheses: R1 duty views (`env.r150` item 4; spec lines 483–495); the
   719	  F-basis rule of spec lines 742–750; the DC chain state (bp F5: one
   720	  height per block; the entry `T_h` is the block that entered h). It does
   721	  not use `a≤f`.
   722	- Statement (registry): let d be an honest duty with view V_d and current
   723	  accepted F = F_d. Let P1 be the greatest `(h_j, J.root)` justified pair
   724	  in V_d whose J is compatible with F (the `fg.frame.v1` rule). Let P2 be
   725	  the lex-greatest such pair with `F ⪯ J` (the `fg.frame.v2` rule). Then
   726	  P1 = P2. The same holds for the FJ frame: the wording "compatible with
   727	  F" of `env.r151` (r151 line 44) and the `F ⪯ σ[W].J` test of
   728	  `fj.frame.v1` select the same pair.
   729	- Proof (registry, 2026-09-28).
   730	  1. Checkpoint heights. A justified pair is `(h, T_h)` of a chain state
   731	     (dc line 824). `T_h` is the block that brought its chain into height
   732	     h (dc lines 747–748, 838), so `σ[T_h].h = h`. A finalized pair is a
   733	     former justified pair (dc line 820). The only exception is the
   734	     initial pair `(0, genesis)`, with `σ[genesis].h = 1` (dc lines
   735	     762–767). Thus each pair `(h,C)` has `h ≤ σ[C].h`, with equality when
   736	     C ≠ genesis. Heights do not decrease along a chain, and a non-genesis
   737	     entry T is the first block of its height on its chain. So every
   738	     strict ancestor of T has state height at most `σ[T].h − 1`.
   739	  2. Part (i): if `h_J ≥ h_F`, then "J is compatible with F" ⇔ `F ⪯ J`.
   740	     The direction ⇐ is immediate. For ⇒, suppose `J ≺ F` strictly. Then
   741	     F ≠ genesis, so `h_F = σ[F].h`, and step 1 gives
   742	     `h_J ≤ σ[J].h ≤ h_F − 1`. This contradicts `h_J ≥ h_F`.
   743	  3. Part (ii): V_d holds a pair with `F ⪯ J` and `h_J ≥ h_F`. If F is
   744	     genesis, every pair has `F ⪯ J` and `h_J ≥ 0 = h_F`. Otherwise
   745	     `update_finality` accepted F only with `σ.F ⪯ Σ.J` (spec line 742).
   746	     The F basis saved the J carrier W0, with `σ[W0].J = Σ.J` (spec lines
   747	     736–739, 749). R1 puts the F basis in every duty view (spec lines
