   574	
   575	**7. Locks and an exact N12 execution**
   576	
   577	F10 — PROVED for an in-band selected source. Let C_fg have height m≥lo
   578	in its full action view. Suppose a lock on J'≠T_c at m suppresses its
   579	height row. Its finality pair required a justification carrier at
   580	height at least m+1. This carrier is retained in the full store.
   581	A same-action finality pair has the same property.
   582	
   583	Since m≤H and lo≥H−1, this gives H=m+1 and lo=m. A strict contest would
   584	give lo=m+1, a contradiction. The lock's J' is compatible with F;
   585	otherwise finalized crossing or source descent from F already excludes
   586	this case. Same-height justification uniqueness gives j=m and J=J'.
   587	The remaining FJ case is uncontested, with root J'. C_fg at height m
   588	must then have entry J'. This contradicts the mismatched lock.
   589	
   590	In a contest, an actual head reaches H. A lock at H would require an
   591	already known carrier at H+1, contrary to the fixed frontier. Locks at
   592	H−1 do not block rows at H. Old different targets cause timeouts there,
   593	which still contribute progress.
   594	
   595	This does not say every action has a source, or that every selected
   596	prefix of a raw result is in band. The no-source and below-band cases
   597	are handled by the producer in §9. F10 alone is not a liveness theorem.
   598	
   599	F11 — REFUTED. Here is N12 with exact receipts, starting from genesis.
   600	The tested variant has FJ's frontier root test, but always uses the
   601	old band {H−1,H}, in both viability and eligibility.
   602	
   603	```text
   604	Δ=16 ticks; n=4; honest u1,u2,u3; faulty b.
   605	q=3; τ=2; k=2; L=7Δ; R=3; P=12Δ; δ_t=6 slots; w_F=2.
   606	GST=60Δ=960 ticks. All honest validators are awake.
   607	b owns slots 1..15. It sends only the blocks specified below.
   608	Every slot ≥16 has honest proposer u1.
   755	```
   756	
   757	This is more than two raw frame changes at one numerical frontier.
   758	It is the same full/frozen distinction as fg-frame-recovery §2.2,
   759	now with FJ's own contest bit. It does not violate the source-reset
   760	theorem: the affected heights in this prefix are at or below M.
   761	
   762	F12 — PROVED for effective changes after relay settling. Fix an honest
   763	archival frontier m during a no-rise interval. After one P margin,
   764	a maximizing witness is in every duty view. Under a≤f there is at
   765	most one justified entry at m−1. There are at most these phases:
   766	
   767	```text
   768	gap: no top J
   769	    -> uncontested top J
   770	    -> contested top J
   771	
   772	or gap -> contested top J.
   773	```
   774	
   775	The first top-J evidence and the first contest evidence can each
   776	interrupt an attempt once. Within P of each event, accepted-object
   777	relay and a later freeze put the relevant evidence in every view.
   778	Repeated copies do not start a new phase. Later frontier blocks only
   779	add witnesses once the phase is settled.
   780	
   781	A finalization below m−1 is below every band witness and cannot cause
   782	an independent exclusion. A finalization at m−1 is the same unique
   783	top J. It is impossible in the contested phase by F2; in the
   784	uncontested phase the root already enforces it. A finalization at m
   785	requires a carrier above m, which ends the no-rise interval.
   786	
   787	Hence k_eff≤2, with at most three complete attempts. This count is
   788	independent of SA's slow-window parameter k. It is not a strictly
   789	increasing potential on each full/HEAD call.
   790	
   791	Split delivery can spend the settling margin. It cannot hold readers
   792	in different phases indefinitely under relay. Source retention in §6

