   549	/-!
   550	# §5.2 Fork choice — `def:fg-candidate-tree`, `alg:fg-store` (PROTOCOL.md `def:fg-candidate-tree`, `alg:fg-store`)
   551	
   552	The composed head: an FG floor and candidate tree, one SG anchor inside it, one
   553	Goldfish walk from that anchor (PROTOCOL.md `alg:sg-fork-choice`).
   554	
   555	```
   556	get_fg_root → get_filtered_block_tree → majority_fork_choice → goldfish_fork_choice
   557	```
   558	
   559	Three things the document leaves to the model.
   560	
   561	* **`goldfish_fork_choice` has to be restated.** The document redefines
   562	  `goldfish_eligible` here (PROTOCOL.md `alg:fg-store`) and leaves
   563	  `goldfish_fork_choice` alone, because the gate is late-bound in its prose.
   564	  Lean resolves it at definition time, so the composition is written again with
   565	  the §5 gate; its body is §2's, letter for letter
   566	  (PROTOCOL.md `alg:goldfish`). The same reason restates the two duties in
   567	  `Attest.lean`.
   568	* **The anchor may sit outside the tree.** `get_fg_root` can return `Σ.J`
   569	  while `get_filtered_block_tree` filters by viability, so the walk's first
   570	  `children` set is computed from an anchor the tree need not hold.
   571	  "Goldfish starts at the root even if the root is not in the filtered tree"
   572	  (PROTOCOL.md `sec:fg-fork-choice`) — `Protocol.ghost` already tests membership on the
   573	  child only, so nothing extra is needed.
   574	* **Available confirmation does not come through here.** It "runs its own walk
   575	  from `Σ.F` over `T_F(Σ)`; it uses neither the candidate tree, the SG root, nor
   576	  the height filter" (PROTOCOL.md#the-complete-protocol). §7 re-anchors it
   577	  (PROTOCOL.md `alg:store`); §5 leaves §2's version alone.
   578	-/
